  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tod und Leben. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tod und Leben (Death and Life) is a simple German card game for two players, similar to War. It is distinct in that players have their own draw piles and must win cards to stay 'alive'. The game ends when one player loses all their cards (Death) and the other has all of them (Life).",
    objective: 'Collect all 32 cards by winning battles: each player reveals the top card of their pile simultaneously; the higher rank takes both cards to the bottom of their pile. On ties, war: each plays one face-down then one face-up; higher face-up wins all. The last player with cards wins (Life); the other loses (Death).',
    gameplay: 'Simultaneous reveal of top card. Higher card wins both. Winner puts cards at bottom of their pile. Ties: War mechanism (play one down, one up, compare).',
    keyRules: [
      'Higher rank wins',
      'Win all cards to win game',
    ],
